@startuml
' Designation: proposed design; accepted in the 2026-10-23 design conversation.
' Supporting specification: ../../.scratch/assignment-workflow/spec.md
' Acceptance and rendering record: README.md
title Proposed design v2 — 1. Intake, solution, and plan
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 420
actor Student
participant "Planning agent" as Agent
participant "Lesson chatbot\n(fresh chat per lesson)" as Tutor

Student -> Agent : Assignment instructions and course materials;\noptional deadline and preferred lesson length
Agent -> Agent : Create separate local assignment workspace\nand Git history outside the public skill repository
Agent -> Student : Confirm interpretation and clarify consequential gaps
opt Material conversion needed
  Agent -> Student : Explain tools, outputs, and fidelity limits; request permission
  Student -> Agent : Approve conversion, or decline
  Agent -> Agent : Run only approved conversions; preserve originals\nand identify remaining information gaps
end
group Stage 1 — Complete the assignment
  Agent -> Agent : Create worked solution using course materials;\ndistinguish external sources and record support
  Agent -> Agent : Check required deliverables and correctness;\nrecord unresolved limitations and save Git version
  Agent -> Student : Make completed worked solution immediately accessible;\nexplain verification results and limitations
end
group Prepare stage 2 — Teach the assignment
  Agent -> Agent : Plan lessons beginning with assignment instructions;\ninclude necessary prerequisites and realistic pacing
  Agent -> Student : Propose lesson plan and flag time constraints
  Student -> Agent : Review and approve plan, with revisions as needed
end
note over Student, Tutor
Continue with the lesson cycle on page 2.
end note

newpage Proposed design v2 — 2. Lesson cycle and final handoff

loop Each lesson, until plan complete or student overrides progression
  Student -> Agent : Request next lesson
  Agent -> Agent : Resolve any outstanding packet: resume, replace,\nor abandon; preserve packet and report history
  Agent -> Agent : Select lesson context; assess packet size\nand extraneous information for the target chatbot
  opt Selected material is too large or includes excessive irrelevant content
    Agent -> Agent : Summarize and/or create trimmed derivative files\n(e.g., a PDF containing only relevant lecture slides)
    Agent -> Agent : Check lesson-critical details are retained; preserve originals\nand record source files, page/slide references, and limitations
  end
  Agent -> Student : Stage self-contained mailbox packet with selected sources,\nsolution context, lesson instructions, and JSON report template
  note over Student, Agent
  One outstanding packet per assignment.
  Packets identify assignment, lesson, and solution version.
  end note
  Student -> Tutor : Manually upload packet to a fresh chatbot session
  opt Useful to gauge prior knowledge
    Tutor -> Student : Short opening assessment
    Student -> Tutor : Answers
  end
  Tutor -> Student : Teach and adapt to demonstrated knowledge;\nask for explanations, justifications, and follow-up answers
  Student -> Tutor : Work through lesson and answer questions
  Tutor -> Student : JSON report: identifiers, solution version, actual answers,\nassistance, understanding evidence, and suspected errors
  Student -> Agent : Manually return report
  Agent -> Agent : Validate report and version relevance;\nrepair malformed reports without inventing evidence
  note over Student, Agent
  Missing evidence may require student input.
  Invalid or stale reports do not automatically establish progress.
  end note
  opt Suspected solution error, from any source
    Agent -> Agent : Investigate against instructions, sources, and reasoning
    opt Error confirmed
      Agent -> Agent : Correct solution and record revertible Git revision;\nreview affected packets, lessons, and prior evidence
      Agent -> Student : Inform student of correction; no permission required
    end
  end
  Agent -> Agent : Update progress and adapt plan from valid evidence
  alt Substantial scope or workload change
    Agent -> Student : Request approval for revised plan
    Student -> Agent : Approve or adjust revision
  else Routine adaptation
    Agent -> Agent : Apply adjustment automatically
  end
  Agent -> Student : Report progress and recommend next step;\nstudent may override progression
end
group Stage 3 — Student creates their own version
  Agent -> Student : Now create your own version of the assignment
end
note over Student, Agent
The prescribed workflow ends here.
No additional phase-three process is specified.
end note
@enduml
